Subject: [PATCH] Re-apply REQ-179's regression test, lost from its own commit
 by 6cb0b1e
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

REQ-179 is archived as completed, but its commit 768c6e2 contains only the
archive move and the checkpoint — the code change it describes is not in it.

Suite update 6cb0b1e landed between the edit and the finalize. A suite update
writes files to disk, so it overwrote the working-tree generate_test.go while
REQ-179's addition was still uncommitted. By the time finalization staged its
declared commit_paths, that path was byte-identical to HEAD and produced no
diff. Nothing failed: the focused test and the whole maintainer gate had already
run green against the pre-overwrite tree, and finalization has no reason to
suspect a declared path that yields no change.

Re-applies the same test from 2ef1246, verbatim, with REQ-179's header. Green in
0.6s. The other two REQs in this run were checked and are unaffected: c64b1ad and
d39e527 both carry their payloads.

Recorded as D-053.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
